WEBVTT

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:03.890
AUGUST 16, A.D. 2096

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:09.650
Miyuki, our trip to Okinawa starts tomorrow.
Are you done getting ready?

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:14.450
No. I can't make up my mind
which clothes to pack.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.700
How about you, Brother?

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:19.080
Actually, I haven't packed yet, either.

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:23.830
I had so many things to take care of
before the break started.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:29.500
All right, why don't we
start getting ready now?

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:30.250
Right.

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:33.840
I'll start packing as soon as I'm done
clearing this away.

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:38.680
Ms. Miyuki, clearing the table
after meals is my job.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:44.100
But you've been busy
helping my brother, Minami.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:47.310
Oh no, I already finished
packing last night.

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:49.730
No need to worry about me.

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:52.780
Please go on and get ready
for your trip, Ms. Miyuki.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:56.820
Ms. Miyuki?

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:00.280
Then, I guess I'll take you up
on that, all right?

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:01.910
Please just leave it to me.

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:13.710
She does look a lot like her.

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:22.430
It's already been four years
since that day.

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:25.730
The Irregular at Magic High School:
Reminiscence Arc

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:31.480
AUGUST 4, A.D. 2092
THE SKIES ABOVE OKINAWA

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:44.580
<i>Ladies and gentlemen, this plane
will be landing at Naha Airport in ten minutes.</i>

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:49.080
<i>Please make sure your seatbelt is on
and gather up your belongings.</i>

00:01:57.470 --> 00:02:00.390
OKINAWA
NAHA AIRPORT

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:04.350
WELCOME TO OKINAWA

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.990
<i>This big brother of mine
makes me uncomfortable.</i>

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:26.250
Thank you for your hard work.

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:36.760
Miyuki, is something the matter?

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:40.010
No, Mother. It's nothing.

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:42.260
You mustn't let it bother you.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:45.260
After all, Tatsuya is your Guardian.

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:49.270
He may be your big brother,
but he's more or less a servant.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:52.650
And you, Miyuki, are his mistress.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.400
Yes.

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:01.660
What is it?

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:03.910
It's nothing.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.740
Then stop staring at me like that!

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:07.910
It's so unpleasant!

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:12.120
I beg your pardon.

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:24.390
<i>I just don't like my big brother.</i>

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:02.720
Welcome, Madam!

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:09.220
I'm so glad that you were also able to make it,
Ms. Miyuki and Master Tatsuya!

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:12.730
Hello, Honami! I know
you'll be taking good care of us here.

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:16.110
Now then, please come inside.

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:18.860
I've got some chilled barley tea.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:21.570
Or would you like me
to brew some hot tea?

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:22.610
Thank you.

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:25.780
Since you've gone to the trouble,
I'll have some barley tea.

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:27.910
All right. As you wish.

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:31.660
Is barley tea all right with you, too,
Ms. Miyuki and Master Tatsuya?

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:33.750
Yes. Thank you very much.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:36.880
Thank you for going to all this trouble.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:48.140
Mother, I think I'll go outside for a walk.

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:50.890
Then please put on some sunscreen.

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:53.640
Since the sunlight in Okinawa
is harsher than on the mainland.

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:58.610
I'll be happy to apply it onto you!

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:00.770
B-But I can do it myself!

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:03.280
Oh, don't be shy! Just leave it to me!

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:08.280
What are you doing, Honami?

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:10.200
You can't have too much protection!

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:13.500
I-I'll take care of my front myself!

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:15.660
Then I'll do this part!

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:18.540
I-I can do my own legs, too!

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:19.540
Now, now...

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:24.670
I-I don't think I need any
inside my skirt!

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:26.550
It's just to be safe!

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:40.310
All right, then, Mother,
I'm going out for a short walk.

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:43.820
Miyuki, take Tatsuya with you.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:49.490
Miyuki?

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:54.830
Very well. I'll be heading out now.

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:10.970
What a lovely breeze!

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:31.490
<i>Really, a Guardian?</i>

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:34.990
<i>As if I need to be escorted
on a mere walk.</i>

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:38.910
<i>In the first place, my bro—</i>

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:42.500
<i>That person's weaker than me!</i>

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:48.470
<i>It's not like he's going to be of any use,
so he shouldn't have to guard me.</i>

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:54.350
<i>I have no need for him to protect me.</i>

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:04.610
<i>If I were to relieve him of his duties,
he could be free.</i>

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:06.860
<i>No...</i>

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:12.820
<i>Even if he were no longer my Guardian,
he wouldn't necessarily be free.</i>

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:19.290
<i>But that alone isn't enough reason
to have him go on being my Guardian.</i>

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:23.880
<i>Why do I feel this way toward him?</i>

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:31.430
<i>When I don't even feel
comfortable around him.</i>

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:33.680
<i>When I don't even like him.</i>

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:42.060
Hey, that hurt.

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:43.980
Where do you think you're going?

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:47.820
<i>Could he be a second-generation Left-Blood?</i>

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:53.820
<i>The guidebook said the children left behind by the
former American occupying forces were miscreants,</i>

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:55.830
<i>so to be careful around them...</i>

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:03.290
Huh? We have no business
with a little punk like you.

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:06.210
So scared, you lost your voice?

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:09.170
Hah! What a chicken!
Stop posing, butthead!

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:14.470
<i>If only I had my CAD with me, I wouldn't
let them get away with talk like that!</i>

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:19.970
I'm not looking for an apology,
so go back to where you came from.

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:22.140
That would be in both our interests.

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:26.900
What did you say?

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:29.650
I'm sure that you heard me.

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:32.150
Get down on your knees
and beg for forgiveness.

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:36.620
Since you were so bold,
I'll look the other way!

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:43.960
<i>Did he use magic?</i>

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:47.290
<i>No, there was no sign of that!</i>

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:50.550
This is getting interesting.

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:53.340
I was only planning to mess with you!

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:57.390
Are you sure? If you take this any further,
you won't be able to laugh it off.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:03.060
<i>Why would you bait him like that?</i>

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:05.480
<i>You have no chance!</i>

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:09.980
For a little punk, you sure know
how to mouth off like a boss!

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:27.670
Hey, Joe!

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:29.540
You've got to be kidding.

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:33.920
Let's head back now.

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:49.360
<i>I never knew that he was this powerful.</i>

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:51.070
Is something the matter?

00:09:52.570 --> 00:09:54.570
No, it's nothing.

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:08.040
The Irregular at Magic High School:
Reminiscence Arc

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:15.170
Welcome back! Ms. Miyuki?

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:19.680
Ms. Miyuki!
Did something happen?

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:24.640
A strange man tried
to pick a fight with me.

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:28.230
But it's all right. That person...

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:31.810
I mean, my brother protected me.

00:10:32.110 --> 00:10:36.030
Did he now?
Well done, Master Tatsuya!

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:39.410
No, I was only carrying out my mission.

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:43.410
Master Tatsuya...

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:47.250
It's commendable that you're aware
of your own place.

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:50.500
Tatsuya, be sure
to keep up the good work.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:58.220
Um, I'm going to take a shower now.

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:11.310
<i>What do you mean by "mission"?</i>

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:13.610
<i>His place?</i>

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:17.690
<i>Did he only protect me
because it was his duty?</i>

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:24.030
<i>Why? Why I am crying?</i>

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:28.700
<i>Why should I be in tears?</i>

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:32.330
<i>Why?</i>

00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:42.720
Ms. Miyuki? It's Honami.

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:45.470
Yes. Come in.

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:50.680
I see that you're ready to go now!

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:53.600
Honami, how's my mother?

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:55.730
She's resting now.

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:59.820
It was just a slight fever,
so I think she'll be fine by tomorrow.

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:01.700
Is that right?

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:05.490
I'd like to stay by my mother's side tonight.

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:08.660
But of course that's not possible, is it?

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:13.500
Tonight's host is the head
of the Kuroba Family,

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:15.710
one of the branch families
of the Yotsuba Clan.

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:19.710
This is an important relationship
for you, too, Ms. Miyuki, so...

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:22.010
I understand that.

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:26.350
After all, I'm the only one
who can serve as my mother's proxy.

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:31.980
That's admirable of you,
but that look of aversion ruins it.

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:33.850
You can tell, then?

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:37.230
Well, to me, it's obvious!

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:41.650
Please don't tease me.

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:42.990
I'm sorry!

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:48.740
But there are plenty of people in the world
who are more perceptive than me.

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:54.120
There might be someone
at tonight's party

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:57.210
who could tell at a glance
that you're averse.

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:00.840
I know it may sound harsh,

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:06.260
but you need to conquer any vulnerabilities
that might discredit you.

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:10.100
What should I do?

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:17.060
What you need

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:21.360
is to become adept at betraying
your own feelings, shall I say?

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:27.360
Your public stance is something
you use to convince yourself first.

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:30.870
That would be difficult.

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:34.660
I wish you could come with me, Honami.

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:39.710
You have Tatsuya on your side,
Miyuki, remember?

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:42.840
Even with him around...

00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:49.600
But isn't it really his job as the eldest son
to maintain a relationship with Uncle Kuroba?

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:53.390
I'm sorry!

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:57.020
You don't have to apologize,
Ms. Miyuki.

00:13:57.350 --> 00:14:00.230
Now then, wipe that look off your face!

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:02.730
It's almost time for you to leave!

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:12.990
Under normal circumstances,
they'd be close as siblings.

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:19.170
Unlike me, Master Tatsuya
is not an Augmented Magician.

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:21.750
He's not a manufactured human.

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:25.670
There's no reason
that he should be a Guardian.

00:14:29.130 --> 00:14:30.470
Madam...

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:36.980
I just don't see their relationship
as being the one they should have.

00:14:53.240 --> 00:14:57.660
Uncle, thank you for inviting us tonight.

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:02.080
Ah, thank you for coming, Miyuki!

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:04.250
How's your mother? Is she all right?

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:06.630
I'm grateful for your concern.

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:10.130
I believe that she's just a little tired,

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:13.350
but we thought we should err
on the side of caution tonight.

00:15:13.970 --> 00:15:16.560
Hearing that sets my mind at ease.

00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:20.520
Well! This is no place
to be having a chat.

00:15:20.900 --> 00:15:23.060
Now then, you can head back there.

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:27.110
Both Ayako and Fumiya
have been looking forward to seeing you.

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:28.280
Go on.

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:45.340
Ayako? Fumiya?

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:47.550
Miyuki!

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:51.050
It's been a long time!

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:52.720
Have you two been well?

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:53.680
Yes!

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:56.140
You're looking well yourself, Miyuki.

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:58.100
Fumiya...

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:01.310
Don't you feel hot,
wearing that outfit?

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:05.060
Oh no! I'm a member
of the Kuroba family, too!

00:16:05.060 --> 00:16:08.480
As such, I must always
be dressed impeccably!

00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:10.190
Truer word never spoken.

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:15.530
Since we heard that our lovely cousin
would be coming,

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:18.580
I've made sure to be dressed
to the nines myself!

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:24.710
FU FU FU...

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:24.710
HO HO HO

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:22.870
<i>So competitive...</i>

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:24.710
Miyuki...

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:27.840
Didn't Tatsuya come with you tonight?

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:30.420
I have him standing by over there.

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:32.050
Tatsuya!

00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:34.640
Really! Well, what can you do?

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:44.230
Seriously...

00:16:44.730 --> 00:16:47.480
Leaving our esteemed guest all alone...

00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:55.870
<i>Wait, he smiled!</i>

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:58.780
<i>Not a tiny smile, not a grimace...</i>

00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:00.490
<i>So naturally!</i>

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:02.330
<i>But why?</i>

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:07.840
<i>He's never smiled at me
like that before!</i>

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:10.960
Now, now, you two... Fumiya, Ayako...

00:17:11.420 --> 00:17:14.260
You mustn't bother Tatsuya
while he's on duty.

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:16.470
Father...

00:17:17.090 --> 00:17:18.510
Thank you for your hard work.

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:20.600
It looks like you're carrying out
your duty as you should.

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:22.980
I appreciate that.

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:25.600
Well, now, Father!

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:28.480
He can spare a few moments, can't he?

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:35.740
I believe it's our job as hosts to make sure
that the guests are in no danger.

00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:41.620
The Kurobas' guards aren't so inept that
they can't guarantee the safety of a single guest!

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:43.700
Isn't that right, Father?

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:46.250
Well, I can't say that you're wrong.

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:49.590
<i>This is probably
what my uncle really wants to say.</i>

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:52.300
<i>To his own children...</i>

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:54.090
<i>Especially to Fumiya...</i>

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:57.720
<i>"You're not to show
any fondness toward that person."</i>

00:17:58.890 --> 00:18:02.310
<i>As the heir apparent to the Yotsuba family,</i>

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:07.940
<i>for Fumiya to idolize the mere bodyguard
of another heir apparent like myself...</i>

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:09.610
<i>That's something to be ashamed of.</i>

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:13.610
<i>He's a servant,
an expendable instrument.</i>

00:18:14.610 --> 00:18:17.610
<i>That's how it is in the Yotsuba clan.</i>

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:21.530
<i>To become "Miyuki Yotsuba,"</i>

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:24.120
<i>I must look at him in the same way.</i>

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:27.370
<i>He's first and foremost my Guardian.</i>

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:30.250
<i>As an instrument...</i>

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:33.630
<i>it's no wonder he has no love for me.</i>

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:37.130
<i>And neither should I harbor any love for him.</i>

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:40.010
<i>My brother is my bodyguard.</i>

00:18:40.010 --> 00:18:42.220
<i>The shield that protects me.</i>

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:44.720
Fumiya?

00:18:45.020 --> 00:18:46.390
Y-Yes?

00:18:46.850 --> 00:18:49.940
Don't put your father
on the spot like that.

00:18:50.310 --> 00:18:51.900
<i>He smiled again!</i>

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:57.150
<i>This won't do! If I seem irritated now,</i>

00:18:57.150 --> 00:19:01.120
<i>my uncle might misunderstand
and think I'm not happy with my brother.</i>

00:19:01.820 --> 00:19:04.370
<i>Would that be a misunderstanding?</i>

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:07.960
<i>No good! I mustn't think such thoughts!</i>

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:13.670
<i>Your public stance is something
that you use to convince yourself first.</i>

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:20.260
Mr. Kuroba, would it be okay
if I left the interior to you?

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:23.180
I'd like to patrol
the perimeter outside.

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:27.310
Oh, is that right?
Well, I must say that's commendable.

00:19:28.310 --> 00:19:30.350
You can leave Miyuki
in our hands, then.

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:34.020
Come on! We can't even have
a good, long chat?

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:37.400
Tatsuya, please be sure
to get back as soon as possible.

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:41.450
Understood. I'll come back
after I sweep the place once.

00:19:39.950 --> 00:19:44.990
<i>My brother is faithfully trying
to fulfill the duty he was tasked with.</i>

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:47.620
<i>That's why I, too,</i>

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:53.170
<i>must faithfully try to act out the role
that I was given, to the utmost.</i>

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:56.170
AUGUST 5, A.D. 2092
THE SOUTHWESTERN WATERS
OFF IEJIMA

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:06.720
I'll take the next one!

00:20:07.890 --> 00:20:11.190
Honami, please take a seat
next to my mother.

00:20:11.190 --> 00:20:12.390
Oh no, I...

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:14.310
Please, I insist.

00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:16.770
Honami, I don't see why not.

00:20:18.900 --> 00:20:21.030
If you say so, Madam.

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:28.290
Honami, please move
a little closer to my mother.

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:34.790
All right! Three, two, one!

00:20:37.550 --> 00:20:40.260
That was such a lovely smile, Honami!

00:20:40.880 --> 00:20:42.510
Thank you very much.

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:45.760
Why don't I take a picture
of you and Master Tatsuya next?

00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:48.760
Oh no, I...

00:20:49.010 --> 00:20:51.640
I don't see why you shouldn't!

00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:53.600
How about you, Master Tatsuya?

00:20:57.770 --> 00:21:00.280
Madam, what should I do?

00:21:02.530 --> 00:21:03.990
Do as you wish.

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:07.160
Well, now that we have
Madam's permission...

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:09.660
Master Tatsuya, please take a seat there.

00:21:15.330 --> 00:21:18.040
Okay! I want to see some smiles now!

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:20.800
Three, two, one!

00:21:35.600 --> 00:21:37.020
What's going on?

00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:38.110
This looks like trouble!

00:21:38.110 --> 00:21:43.490
A submarine-like shadow
is approaching from the stern!

00:21:43.780 --> 00:21:46.240
Violating territorial waters by submarine?

00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:48.450
Are they planning to start a war?

00:21:48.990 --> 00:21:51.080
Madam, please take refuge in your cabin!

00:21:51.450 --> 00:21:54.580
Ms. Miyuki, please stay with Madam!

00:21:54.830 --> 00:21:56.460
Oh, right!

00:22:06.340 --> 00:22:08.390
Let me help, too!

00:22:11.140 --> 00:22:13.430
<i>Without a CAD?</i>

00:22:13.770 --> 00:22:17.770
<i>I know that magic isn't your thing,
but you are a magician, aren't you?</i>

00:22:20.860 --> 00:22:22.530
Is that... Don't tell me!

00:22:22.820 --> 00:22:24.190
Torpedoes?

00:22:30.830 --> 00:22:32.740
<i>What is he planning to do?</i>

00:23:01.310 --> 00:23:03.650
<i>What just happened?</i>

00:23:04.690 --> 00:23:07.280
<i>Was that magic just now?</i>

00:23:07.610 --> 00:23:09.700
<i>Without a CAD...</i>

00:23:09.700 --> 00:23:12.530
<i>What in the world? And how?</i>

00:23:13.030 --> 00:23:18.120
<i>He was able to use magic, then?
Such advanced magic as that?</i>

00:23:18.120 --> 00:23:21.170
<i>He's been pretending
not to be able to use magic?</i>

00:23:22.840 --> 00:23:24.800
<i>Who are you?</i>

00:23:26.010 --> 00:23:28.380
<i>I don't know a thing...</i>

00:23:29.550 --> 00:23:31.590
<i>about this person.</i>

00:23:48.110 --> 00:23:51.070
AUGUST 5, A.D. 2092

00:23:49.070 --> 00:23:51.570
All right, let me ask you again.

00:23:52.110 --> 00:23:55.030
You say that torpedoes were fired
at you from the submarine,

00:23:55.030 --> 00:23:58.950
but do you have any idea
why that happened?

00:23:59.500 --> 00:24:01.620
I've told you over and over!

00:24:01.620 --> 00:24:03.630
We have no idea whatsoever!

00:24:08.050 --> 00:24:09.510
Captain?

00:24:10.130 --> 00:24:12.890
Don't you think
this has gone on long enough?

00:24:13.180 --> 00:24:18.640
I doubt that we have
anything useful to tell you.

00:24:19.390 --> 00:24:20.940
Is that right?

00:24:23.190 --> 00:24:25.900
Thank you for your cooperation.

00:24:33.740 --> 00:24:34.910
I see.

00:24:35.240 --> 00:24:39.160
So you're the boy
who knocked Joe flat on his back?

00:24:41.210 --> 00:24:46.590
You're extraordinarily gifted if you've mastered
the counterstrike at such a young age.

00:24:47.710 --> 00:24:49.170
Lance Corporal Higaki!

00:24:55.010 --> 00:25:00.180
My subordinate was disrespectful
to you yesterday. He'd like to apologize.

00:25:01.020 --> 00:25:03.440
I am Lance Corporal Joseph Higaki!

00:25:03.770 --> 00:25:06.690
I was extremely disrespectful
to you yesterday.

00:25:11.240 --> 00:25:13.070
Apology accepted.

00:25:13.700 --> 00:25:15.530
Thank you very much.

00:25:23.120 --> 00:25:24.960
Tatsuya Shiba, was it?

00:25:25.540 --> 00:25:31.420
Currently, I'm also serving as the instructor
for the Airborne Magicians Unit at Onna Base.

00:25:31.960 --> 00:25:35.300
If you can find the time,
I'd like you to visit the base.

00:25:36.050 --> 00:25:38.800
I'm sure that you'll find it interesting.

00:25:40.430 --> 00:25:41.560
Now then...

00:25:45.900 --> 00:25:47.060
Drive.

00:25:52.070 --> 00:25:54.570
AUGUST 6, A.D. 2092

00:26:22.720 --> 00:26:25.270
What would you like to do today?

00:26:27.190 --> 00:26:30.110
It's probably not a good day
for shopping.

00:26:30.980 --> 00:26:32.480
What shall we do?

00:26:33.650 --> 00:26:35.610
Let's see.

00:26:39.110 --> 00:26:41.990
How about seeing a Ryukyu dance performance?

00:26:42.870 --> 00:26:45.870
I hear that you can also try it
yourself in costume.

00:26:46.460 --> 00:26:48.420
I think I'd enjoy that.

00:26:49.380 --> 00:26:51.880
What do you think, Miyuki?

00:26:52.380 --> 00:26:55.630
Yes, I think I'd enjoy that, too.

00:26:57.420 --> 00:27:00.760
Then, I'll arrange for car service.
The only thing is...

00:27:01.680 --> 00:27:04.640
it seems to be open only to women.

00:27:05.140 --> 00:27:06.520
I see.

00:27:07.520 --> 00:27:08.270
Tatsuya?

00:27:09.980 --> 00:27:11.020
Yes?

00:27:12.310 --> 00:27:16.780
You were invited to the base
by that captain yesterday, weren't you?

00:27:17.320 --> 00:27:20.030
It would be a good opportunity
for you, so take a tour.

00:27:20.570 --> 00:27:24.660
They might even allow you
to take part in the drills.

00:27:25.330 --> 00:27:27.040
I will do as you say.

00:27:28.040 --> 00:27:29.920
Excuse me... Mother?

00:27:30.370 --> 00:27:31.880
I, too...

00:27:33.920 --> 00:27:38.010
W-Would it be all right
if I went with my brother?

00:27:38.550 --> 00:27:40.050
Miyuki?

00:27:40.380 --> 00:27:47.430
Um, I'd be interested to see what kind of training
the magicians on base go through. And...

00:27:48.350 --> 00:27:53.900
as his mistress, I should know
what my own Guardian's skill level is.

00:27:54.480 --> 00:27:57.190
Is that right? I'm impressed.

00:27:57.940 --> 00:28:02.820
But for now, at least publicly,
you two are brother and sister.

00:28:05.410 --> 00:28:07.830
Tatsuya, it is just as you heard.

00:28:08.160 --> 00:28:11.460
Miyuki will accompany you
on your tour of the base.

00:28:11.460 --> 00:28:12.080
Right.

00:28:12.790 --> 00:28:16.460
During today's outing,
you are to behave like siblings.

00:28:16.750 --> 00:28:20.550
Rather than "Ms.,"
you are to address Miyuki as "Miyuki,"

00:28:20.930 --> 00:28:22.720
and avoid speaking deferentially.

00:28:22.720 --> 00:28:24.010
Understood.

00:28:24.010 --> 00:28:26.310
Are we clear, as well, Miyuki?

00:28:26.310 --> 00:28:27.470
Oh, yes!

00:28:49.540 --> 00:28:52.620
I'm Sanada of Weapons Development.

00:28:53.250 --> 00:28:54.830
I'm Tatsuya Shiba.

00:28:54.830 --> 00:28:56.880
Thank you for today's tour.

00:28:57.210 --> 00:29:00.880
I'm his little sister, Miyuki Shiba.
Thank you for having us.

00:29:01.470 --> 00:29:03.930
Well, that's polite of you.

00:29:03.930 --> 00:29:05.970
We welcome you to our base.

00:29:05.970 --> 00:29:07.510
Now then, come inside.

00:29:10.520 --> 00:29:13.020
One! Two!

00:29:13.810 --> 00:29:17.520
Run! You're going slow!

00:29:17.980 --> 00:29:19.020
Next!

00:29:19.020 --> 00:29:20.780
- That's it?
- Is that all you've got?

00:29:20.780 --> 00:29:22.360
Move your feet!

00:29:22.360 --> 00:29:25.240
Don't slack off because it's a drill!

00:29:25.240 --> 00:29:26.740
Do what you'd do in actual combat!

00:29:27.620 --> 00:29:29.790
Welcome to Onna Base.

00:29:30.200 --> 00:29:36.040
Since you came here so soon, may I take it
that you have an interest in the military?

00:29:36.040 --> 00:29:37.420
I am interested...

00:29:37.840 --> 00:29:41.420
but I haven't decided yet
whether or not I'm going to become a soldier.

00:29:41.960 --> 00:29:45.930
Well, can't say that I blame you.
Are you still in middle school?

00:29:46.550 --> 00:29:48.720
I just started middle school.

00:29:49.010 --> 00:29:51.430
You're grounded for your age.

00:29:51.430 --> 00:29:52.640
Thank you.

00:29:52.980 --> 00:29:56.060
Um, everyone here is a magician, right?

00:29:56.650 --> 00:30:01.570
Yes, but as in some cases, they might not be
able to use their CADs on the battlefield.

00:30:02.320 --> 00:30:05.820
They're training so that they can use
the bare minimum of magic...

00:30:05.820 --> 00:30:09.700
needed for their combat strategies.

00:30:14.750 --> 00:30:17.170
Next up is elimination-style matches.

00:30:18.630 --> 00:30:20.840
As long as they only use
their bare hands, it's anything goes.

00:30:21.590 --> 00:30:24.340
They fight one-on-one
and keep going until they lose.

00:30:28.010 --> 00:30:29.010
Next!

00:30:31.470 --> 00:30:36.600
Shiba, I bet just watching
isn't much fun. Want to join in?

00:30:40.230 --> 00:30:44.190
Yes. Since you're offering,
I'd like to take you up on that.

00:30:46.240 --> 00:30:47.320
Sergeant Toguchi!

00:30:47.990 --> 00:30:48.820
Sir!

00:30:49.200 --> 00:30:51.910
You take on Shiba in a match.

00:30:52.240 --> 00:30:53.700
Understood!

00:30:54.870 --> 00:30:57.460
Shiba, there's no need to hold back.

00:30:57.460 --> 00:31:02.710
As a student, Sergeant Toguchi
was a boxer at the national level.

00:31:10.760 --> 00:31:12.300
Please take me on.

00:31:12.300 --> 00:31:14.470
Right. Go easy on me, okay?

00:31:29.950 --> 00:31:31.820
Well, well...

00:31:34.490 --> 00:31:36.000
Corporal Haebaru!

00:31:36.000 --> 00:31:36.700
Sir!

00:31:36.910 --> 00:31:39.670
Don't think about pulling
your punches. Go full throttle!

00:31:39.670 --> 00:31:40.710
Sir!

00:31:53.930 --> 00:31:56.220
He fights like
it's actual combat, doesn't he?

00:31:56.850 --> 00:32:02.060
Seeing that Corporal Haebaru is well-versed
in both weapons and Okinawa karate,

00:32:02.060 --> 00:32:04.980
he's giving him a wide berth
as he evades his blows.

00:32:05.360 --> 00:32:09.860
That must be out of the assumption
that he's concealing a weapon.

00:32:09.860 --> 00:32:11.240
Yes, probably.

00:32:23.790 --> 00:32:24.920
Match over!

00:32:31.050 --> 00:32:34.430
I had no idea you were at this level.

00:32:34.970 --> 00:32:37.430
He really is something else.

00:32:39.230 --> 00:32:44.440
Still, this leaves the Airborne Corps
on a path to utter disgrace.

00:32:44.980 --> 00:32:47.610
Could you indulge us in one more match?

00:32:47.610 --> 00:32:48.860
How self-serving!

00:32:51.610 --> 00:32:53.860
Please let me take him on.

00:32:54.240 --> 00:32:58.740
Lance Corporal Higaki,
if this is for revenge, I can't allow it.

00:32:59.290 --> 00:33:02.250
It's not for revenge!
It's for vindication!

00:33:03.040 --> 00:33:07.750
Shiba, you heard him.
Will you humor us and face off against him?

00:33:08.130 --> 00:33:13.010
Lance Corporal Higaki may be young,
but he's as fierce as Haebaru.

00:33:13.590 --> 00:33:15.010
I'll take him on.

00:33:17.180 --> 00:33:19.520
B-Brother, are you serious?

00:33:22.520 --> 00:33:24.100
I'll be fine.

00:33:48.880 --> 00:33:51.550
Using magic... That's outrageous!

00:33:52.210 --> 00:33:53.300
Stop it, Miyuki!

00:33:54.880 --> 00:33:58.550
If you're a magician,
using magic in combat is a given.

00:33:59.430 --> 00:34:01.560
<i>Did he just call me "Miyuki"?</i>

00:34:24.250 --> 00:34:26.710
<i>Gram Demolition?</i>

00:34:30.380 --> 00:34:32.710
I'm beat. You trounced me.

00:34:36.430 --> 00:34:40.100
The other day, that wasn't a matter
of me letting my guard down.

00:34:40.100 --> 00:34:41.640
You drove that home, all right.

00:34:42.430 --> 00:34:44.770
Allow me to introduce myself again.

00:34:45.430 --> 00:34:48.980
I'm with the Airborne Corps,
National Defense Force.

00:34:48.980 --> 00:34:51.400
Lance Corporal Joseph Higaki.

00:34:53.190 --> 00:34:54.780
I'm Tatsuya Shiba.

00:34:56.450 --> 00:34:58.280
Okay, Tatsuya!

00:34:58.280 --> 00:35:02.540
You can call me "Joe." You'll be here
in Okinawa for a few more days, right?

00:35:03.240 --> 00:35:05.620
Give me a call if you ever get bored.

00:35:05.620 --> 00:35:09.250
You'd be surprised
at how much pull I have around here!

00:35:09.250 --> 00:35:11.040
That's enough, Joe.

00:35:11.670 --> 00:35:13.550
Training is still in session.

00:35:15.630 --> 00:35:17.680
Sorry to put you on the spot like that.

00:35:17.680 --> 00:35:20.550
It looks like it dispelled
my subordinate's grudge.

00:35:21.010 --> 00:35:24.430
Would you mind joining me for some tea?

00:35:24.770 --> 00:35:29.230
I'd like to hear about that distance strike
you just showed us.

00:35:29.810 --> 00:35:33.480
And please take a look at the CADs
that I've been developing.

00:35:35.990 --> 00:35:37.190
What's this?

00:35:40.950 --> 00:35:42.620
Don't look at me!

00:35:45.950 --> 00:35:48.080
The Irregular at Magic High School:
Reminiscence Arc

00:35:48.210 --> 00:35:51.080
AUGUST 11, A.D. 2092

00:36:02.180 --> 00:36:04.100
<i>He's been doing that all morning.</i>

00:36:04.720 --> 00:36:06.600
<i>Doesn't he get tired of it?</i>

00:36:07.100 --> 00:36:08.100
Ms. Miyuki?

00:36:09.640 --> 00:36:11.230
It's time for lunch.

00:36:12.810 --> 00:36:14.230
Right.

00:36:23.950 --> 00:36:25.030
Thank you.

00:36:25.030 --> 00:36:25.870
Oh no.

00:36:39.510 --> 00:36:42.340
<i>This is an alert
from the National Defense Force.</i>

00:36:43.010 --> 00:36:46.140
<i>While traveling 10 km
east of Tonakijima,</i>

00:36:46.140 --> 00:36:51.060
<i>a Japanese patrol boat came under attack
by a submarine of unknown origin</i>

00:36:51.060 --> 00:36:52.770
<i>and has gone missing.</i>

00:36:53.560 --> 00:36:56.440
<i>Our forces were deployed immediately,</i>

00:36:56.440 --> 00:36:59.650
<i>but we have yet to apprehend
or sink the vessel.</i>

00:37:00.440 --> 00:37:03.660
<i>The Kerama Islands have been subjected
to a missile attack from the sea...</i>

00:37:03.910 --> 00:37:06.660
<i>and the port facilities
have suffered damage.</i>

00:37:06.660 --> 00:37:11.370
<i>We urge those of you watching this broadcast
now to follow the emergency manual</i>

00:37:11.370 --> 00:37:15.630
<i>and start the evacuation process
quickly and calmly.</i>

00:37:15.630 --> 00:37:17.960
<i>Repeat. This is an alert from...</i>

00:37:17.960 --> 00:37:19.170
Madam...

00:37:21.800 --> 00:37:23.930
I've received a phone call
from Captain Kazama of Onna Base,

00:37:23.930 --> 00:37:28.060
suggesting that we evacuate
to the shelter on base.

00:37:38.570 --> 00:37:39.650
Yes?

00:37:40.650 --> 00:37:41.740
Yes.

00:37:42.610 --> 00:37:44.570
Understood.

00:37:48.870 --> 00:37:51.450
Madam, you have a call from Ms. Maya.

00:37:57.710 --> 00:37:59.590
Hello, Maya?

00:38:00.340 --> 00:38:02.470
Sister? It's been a while.

00:38:02.920 --> 00:38:06.180
Things certainly seem
to be hectic down there.

00:38:06.510 --> 00:38:08.470
<i>Yes, you're right about that.</i>

00:38:09.060 --> 00:38:12.020
<i>Have you heard from Captain Kazama?</i>

00:38:12.020 --> 00:38:13.930
About the shelter on base?

00:38:14.270 --> 00:38:17.730
I see. So it was you
who pulled those strings.

00:38:17.730 --> 00:38:19.190
Thank you.

00:38:19.650 --> 00:38:24.990
But as the enemy forces' target,
wouldn't the base actually be more dangerous?

00:38:24.990 --> 00:38:31.330
<i>We're talking about an enemy that wouldn't bother
with rules like "never attack non-military facilities."</i>

00:38:31.330 --> 00:38:37.000
<i>The fact that they'd stoop to anything
surely isn't lost on you, Sister.</i>

00:38:38.670 --> 00:38:40.000
That's true.

00:38:40.500 --> 00:38:41.920
Very well.

00:38:42.250 --> 00:38:45.050
<i>I'm relieved
you're quick to understand.</i>

00:38:45.050 --> 00:38:48.180
<i>Also, do you mind
one more piece of advice?</i>

00:38:48.180 --> 00:38:49.600
No, go right ahead.

00:38:49.800 --> 00:38:51.760
<i>Circumstances being what they are...</i>

00:38:52.770 --> 00:38:56.350
<i>I believe that you should release Tatsuya.</i>

00:38:56.810 --> 00:38:59.020
Are you being serious?

00:38:59.520 --> 00:39:03.940
<i>What I mean is, you should disable
his limiter temporarily.</i>

00:39:03.940 --> 00:39:08.860
<i>I'm sure you can manipulate him at will
without lifting a finger, can't you?</i>

00:39:08.860 --> 00:39:12.790
If you feel so strongly about it,
then I have no objection.

00:39:13.330 --> 00:39:16.040
I think it would be better if you did so.

00:39:16.040 --> 00:39:18.620
As the head of the Yotsuba clan.

00:39:20.040 --> 00:39:23.050
<i>All right, Sister, please be careful.</i>

00:39:23.050 --> 00:39:25.300
Right. Thank you.

00:39:29.090 --> 00:39:31.850
Madam, what did Ms. Maya say?

00:39:32.510 --> 00:39:36.930
It seems that she was the one
who arranged for us to shelter on-base.

00:39:37.480 --> 00:39:40.480
Then, the phone call
that Master Tatsuya received?

00:39:40.480 --> 00:39:42.690
That's what that was about.

00:39:43.230 --> 00:39:44.190
Tatsuya?

00:39:44.400 --> 00:39:45.480
Yes?

00:39:45.480 --> 00:39:49.240
Tell the captain
that we'll be accepting his offer.

00:39:49.570 --> 00:39:52.530
And ask them
to send someone to pick us up.

00:39:52.530 --> 00:39:54.450
Understood.

00:40:07.340 --> 00:40:09.340
I'm Lance Corporal Higaki.

00:40:10.840 --> 00:40:14.680
For now, I'll be taking you
to the break room on the second floor.

00:40:20.600 --> 00:40:23.980
I'll take you to the shelter
as soon as all preparations are complete.

00:40:24.270 --> 00:40:26.980
Please wait here for the time being.

00:40:40.000 --> 00:40:43.250
Madam, don't you find this odd?

00:40:43.580 --> 00:40:45.130
About the shelter?

00:40:45.130 --> 00:40:45.750
Yes.

00:40:46.460 --> 00:40:50.550
There's no point in having a shelter
unless it can be used in an emergency.

00:40:50.550 --> 00:40:53.180
What kind of preparations
do they have to take?

00:40:53.840 --> 00:40:55.010
True.

00:40:55.550 --> 00:41:01.190
Perhaps, they need time to gloss over the fact
that the higher-ups scrambled to get in there first.

00:41:01.600 --> 00:41:03.690
It's going to be all right, Miyuki.

00:41:06.610 --> 00:41:08.280
I've got your back.

00:41:08.940 --> 00:41:10.440
<i>"Miyuki"?</i>

00:41:10.440 --> 00:41:11.610
<i>He...</i>

00:41:11.610 --> 00:41:14.780
<i>My brother just called me "Miyuki" again!</i>

00:41:15.830 --> 00:41:17.700
<i>Speaking so nonchalantly!</i>

00:41:17.700 --> 00:41:20.710
<i>What does he mean,
it'll be all right because he has my back?</i>

00:41:20.710 --> 00:41:23.080
<i>How can he be so sure of that?</i>

00:41:24.670 --> 00:41:28.050
<i>But that's against the rules!</i>

00:41:32.800 --> 00:41:34.800
Master Tatsuya, what was that?

00:41:34.800 --> 00:41:36.550
I think they were gunshots.

00:41:41.930 --> 00:41:43.690
Do you know what's going on?

00:41:43.690 --> 00:41:45.560
No. Not from here.

00:41:53.860 --> 00:41:57.320
There seems to be something
that inhibits magic in this room.

00:41:57.870 --> 00:42:01.080
But it doesn't seem
like you can't use magic at all.

00:42:01.830 --> 00:42:04.580
Tatsuya, go check on
what's happening outside.

00:42:05.170 --> 00:42:07.960
But since the situation is unknown,

00:42:07.960 --> 00:42:10.840
we cannot ignore
the risk of danger in this room.

00:42:10.840 --> 00:42:14.260
If the enemy infiltrates,
I wouldn't be able to protect Miyuki—

00:42:14.260 --> 00:42:15.550
Miyuki?

00:42:16.260 --> 00:42:18.720
Tatsuya, don't forget who you are!

00:42:21.270 --> 00:42:22.480
I beg your pardon.

00:42:36.030 --> 00:42:38.990
You can leave this room
in Honami's hands.

00:42:38.990 --> 00:42:40.870
Understood.

00:42:41.370 --> 00:42:44.160
Sakurai, I'm leaving this to you.

00:42:44.460 --> 00:42:46.370
Right, you can count on me.

00:42:46.370 --> 00:42:48.460
You be careful, too, Tatsuya.

00:43:10.770 --> 00:43:11.650
Excuse me.

00:43:13.570 --> 00:43:17.530
I'm PFC Kinjou
of the Airborne Corps, Second Unit.

00:43:18.240 --> 00:43:20.870
I will now show you
to the underground shelter.

00:43:20.870 --> 00:43:22.280
Please follow me.

00:43:23.290 --> 00:43:27.920
Excuse me. Someone from our group
just stepped out to check outside.

00:43:28.420 --> 00:43:32.170
But some of the enemy forces
have already infiltrated the base.

00:43:32.420 --> 00:43:34.710
It would be dangerous to stay here.

00:43:34.960 --> 00:43:39.430
In that case,
please escort those people first.

00:43:39.680 --> 00:43:40.760
But...

00:43:41.260 --> 00:43:43.680
You... Did you say your name was Kinjou?

00:43:43.680 --> 00:43:46.180
You heard the lady.

00:43:46.180 --> 00:43:49.230
So at least take us there first.

00:43:52.270 --> 00:43:54.570
Madam, if you're worried
about Master Tatsuya,

00:43:54.570 --> 00:43:58.950
I think he could join us
if he went through Captain Kazama.

00:43:58.950 --> 00:44:02.580
It's not as if I'm worried
about Tatsuya.

00:44:03.200 --> 00:44:04.830
That was just an excuse.

00:44:05.160 --> 00:44:05.950
Then...

00:44:07.200 --> 00:44:10.210
I have a feeling
that we can't trust them.

00:44:12.540 --> 00:44:13.210
Dick!

00:44:31.230 --> 00:44:32.270
Mother!

00:44:36.860 --> 00:44:39.240
Dick! Al! Mark! Ben!

00:44:39.240 --> 00:44:41.700
Why? Why did you double-cross me?

00:44:41.990 --> 00:44:45.200
What about you, Joe?
Why so loyal to Japan?

00:44:46.120 --> 00:44:50.460
Have you lost your mind, Dick?
Japan's our homeland for heaven's sake!

00:44:51.000 --> 00:44:53.210
And how has Japan treated us?

00:44:53.790 --> 00:44:57.210
We can join their army
and work for Japan...

00:44:57.760 --> 00:45:00.680
but in the end,
we're still Left-Bloods!

00:45:00.680 --> 00:45:03.720
They never stopped
treating us like outsiders!

00:45:04.850 --> 00:45:06.600
That's all in your head!

00:45:07.180 --> 00:45:08.600
The army, the unit...

00:45:09.140 --> 00:45:11.600
They treat us as their comrades!

00:45:11.890 --> 00:45:14.520
They accept us as their friends!

00:45:15.020 --> 00:45:17.860
Joe! That's because you're a magician!

00:45:19.400 --> 00:45:25.370
The army kisses up to you
because you have your use as a magician!

00:45:25.780 --> 00:45:26.830
Dick...

00:45:27.160 --> 00:45:29.160
Do you really mean that?

00:45:30.290 --> 00:45:35.290
You're outraged at being treated like outsiders
because we're Left-Bloods,

00:45:35.630 --> 00:45:37.000
but you're saying that...

00:45:37.500 --> 00:45:40.260
because I'm a magician,
I'm not one of you?

00:45:40.760 --> 00:45:43.130
Are you saying
that I'm not your friend?

00:45:43.680 --> 00:45:44.930
Dick...

00:45:47.100 --> 00:45:48.390
Joe...

00:45:53.480 --> 00:45:54.560
<i>Now's my chance!</i>

00:46:06.410 --> 00:46:10.790
<i>Mental Interference Magic... Cocytus.</i>

00:46:11.790 --> 00:46:13.750
Hey! Mark!

00:46:16.790 --> 00:46:18.540
You damn magician!

00:46:45.910 --> 00:46:46.950
Miyuki!

00:46:47.620 --> 00:46:48.320
Miyuki!

00:46:58.290 --> 00:46:59.380
Miyuki...

00:47:00.590 --> 00:47:02.800
I'm not going to let you die!

00:47:06.720 --> 00:47:08.140
Come back!

00:47:11.640 --> 00:47:12.970
<i>I'm so cold.</i>

00:47:15.270 --> 00:47:17.940
<i>So, I'm going to die.</i>

00:47:22.190 --> 00:47:22.940
Miyuki...

00:47:25.700 --> 00:47:27.820
Stay with me, Miyuki!

00:47:29.740 --> 00:47:32.200
<i>This voice... My brother?</i>

00:47:33.490 --> 00:47:36.620
<i>Are you sorry to see me go?</i>

00:47:37.540 --> 00:47:42.210
<i>But I've done nothing
but awful things to you.</i>

00:47:42.550 --> 00:47:44.800
Miyuki, Miyuki...

00:47:43.840 --> 00:47:49.680
<i>Before I die, I wish I could've at least
told him that I was sorry.</i>

00:47:45.340 --> 00:47:46.720
Miyuki!

00:47:50.430 --> 00:47:52.890
<i>But no...</i>

00:47:53.600 --> 00:47:57.270
<i>I have no strength.</i>

00:48:29.380 --> 00:48:31.430
<i>I'm being replenished.</i>

00:48:31.890 --> 00:48:34.680
<i>I'm being remade.</i>

00:48:44.770 --> 00:48:46.940
<i>Is this magic?</i>

00:48:48.030 --> 00:48:50.030
<i>Is this really magic?</i>

00:48:59.080 --> 00:49:02.080
<i>Such wonderful power!</i>

00:49:02.080 --> 00:49:04.000
<i>How wonderful he is!</i>

00:49:04.000 --> 00:49:05.670
<i>My...</i>

00:49:14.680 --> 00:49:17.100
...brother...

00:49:17.640 --> 00:49:18.890
Miyuki...

00:49:18.890 --> 00:49:20.100
Thank goodness!

00:49:50.340 --> 00:49:51.880
Brother!

00:50:02.390 --> 00:50:04.270
<i>Her wounds are healing!</i>

00:50:04.690 --> 00:50:06.480
<i>Even the hole in her clothes!</i>

00:50:07.820 --> 00:50:08.980
Mother!

00:50:27.130 --> 00:50:29.840
Didn't I get shot?

00:50:30.460 --> 00:50:32.090
It's thanks to my brother.

00:50:32.590 --> 00:50:34.260
To Master Tatsuya?

00:50:34.260 --> 00:50:37.850
But I don't think those wounds
could've been fixed by Healing Magic.

00:50:38.140 --> 00:50:41.100
It's possible for my brother.

00:50:41.930 --> 00:50:45.440
<i>After all, he's my brother!</i>

00:50:53.280 --> 00:50:56.360
Sorry. Our unit spawning
those insurgents...

00:50:56.700 --> 00:50:58.820
That's totally on us.

00:50:59.200 --> 00:51:02.240
I can't think of any way
that we can atone for that,

00:51:02.240 --> 00:51:06.000
but the National Defense Force will do
everything in its power to accommodate you.

00:51:06.500 --> 00:51:09.210
First of all, if you could explain
what happened exactly...

00:51:09.210 --> 00:51:13.010
So the insurgents' target
was that other family?

00:51:13.840 --> 00:51:18.010
That's right. That man is the CEO
of one of the military's top clients...

00:51:18.300 --> 00:51:21.760
and the insurgents
were looking to take him hostage.

00:51:22.520 --> 00:51:24.810
So we were collateral damage?

00:51:24.810 --> 00:51:27.810
About that... I don't know
how to apologize for that, either.

00:51:27.810 --> 00:51:32.780
No, actually I'm relieved to know
that we weren't the ones they were after.

00:51:33.190 --> 00:51:36.400
So, what about the status
of the infiltration and counterattack?

00:51:36.780 --> 00:51:41.030
The enemy is sending multiple amphibious
crafts toward the Onno Village shoreline.

00:51:41.410 --> 00:51:45.620
The enemy has command of the waters
near the Kerama Islands.

00:51:45.620 --> 00:51:49.380
Thanks to the work of guerillas
colluding with the enemy,

00:51:49.380 --> 00:51:53.050
crew members
are being thwarted in transit.

00:51:53.420 --> 00:51:56.510
About 80% of the guerillas
have been wiped out.

00:51:56.510 --> 00:52:01.430
The Airborne Unit on this base will be mobilizing
soon to counter the enemy ground troops.

00:52:01.760 --> 00:52:03.970
I understand the situation now.

00:52:03.970 --> 00:52:09.690
Next, I'd like you to shelter my mother,
my sister and Sakurai where they'll be safest.

00:52:10.480 --> 00:52:12.570
We'll take them
to the Air Defense Command Room.

00:52:12.570 --> 00:52:13.820
Thank you very much.

00:52:14.280 --> 00:52:18.900
Lastly, please lend me an armor suit
and a set of infantry equipment.

00:52:19.910 --> 00:52:20.910
What for?

00:52:21.410 --> 00:52:24.660
They killed Miyuki.

00:52:25.290 --> 00:52:28.660
I have to make them pay for that.

00:52:30.250 --> 00:52:31.670
Are you planning to go alone?

00:52:32.840 --> 00:52:36.300
Because what I'm after is personal revenge.

00:52:36.920 --> 00:52:39.300
Even if you fight
with vengeance on your mind,

00:52:39.300 --> 00:52:41.890
as long as you have it under control,
it should be fine.

00:52:42.140 --> 00:52:46.390
I just can't allow you to massacre
non-combatants or those who've surrendered.

00:52:46.390 --> 00:52:49.890
I'm not giving them time to surrender.

00:52:50.190 --> 00:52:51.400
Fine, then.

00:52:51.400 --> 00:52:56.280
Our original mission was to either
repulse or annihilate invading forces.

00:52:56.280 --> 00:52:58.780
There's no need to urge
the enemy to surrender, either.

00:52:59.200 --> 00:53:03.410
Young Tatsuya Shiba,
I'm adding you to our battle lines.

00:53:03.700 --> 00:53:06.490
I don't intend to follow
the military's orders.

00:53:06.490 --> 00:53:11.540
Since what I have to protect
and what you have to protect are different things.

00:53:12.080 --> 00:53:16.170
That said, if we share
the goal of annihilating the enemy,

00:53:16.170 --> 00:53:18.050
then let us fight side by side.

00:53:19.800 --> 00:53:23.930
Sanada, set Shiba up with an armor suit
and equipment for hand-to-hand combat.

00:53:24.180 --> 00:53:26.720
The Airborne Unit will be mobilizing
in ten minutes.

00:53:26.720 --> 00:53:27.680
Yes, sir!

00:53:27.680 --> 00:53:29.310
This way, Shiba.

00:53:34.480 --> 00:53:37.690
Sakurai, please look after
my mother and sister.

00:53:48.620 --> 00:53:50.200
Wait a minute, please! Brother!

00:53:55.210 --> 00:53:56.960
What's wrong, Miyuki?

00:53:57.340 --> 00:54:00.210
P-Please don't go!

00:54:02.930 --> 00:54:04.800
Heading out to battle...

00:54:04.800 --> 00:54:06.800
No matter how you look at it,
that's too dangerous!

00:54:06.800 --> 00:54:09.970
Surely there's no need
for you to take such a risk!

00:54:11.640 --> 00:54:13.600
We'll be waiting outside.

00:54:18.730 --> 00:54:20.990
It's true that there's no need.

00:54:21.530 --> 00:54:23.320
This is what I want.

00:54:23.570 --> 00:54:26.320
I won't let anyone
get away with hurting you.

00:54:26.740 --> 00:54:29.870
I'll eliminate everyone who causes you harm.

00:54:30.410 --> 00:54:31.870
Brother...

00:54:33.620 --> 00:54:36.710
I'll never be satisfied unless I do that.

00:54:37.210 --> 00:54:41.260
Because for me, the only thing
that I can truly consider dear to me...

00:54:41.260 --> 00:54:43.970
Miyuki... It's only you.

00:54:45.220 --> 00:54:48.470
That you can consider dear to you?

00:54:49.060 --> 00:54:50.600
You got me.

00:54:51.640 --> 00:54:53.730
I guess it's about time you found out.

00:54:55.020 --> 00:54:59.610
Though I would've kept you in the dark
forever if that were an option.

00:54:59.980 --> 00:55:01.860
Right now, there's no time,

00:55:01.860 --> 00:55:05.280
and besides, I don't think
I should be the one to tell you.

00:55:05.570 --> 00:55:08.910
So Miyuki, have my mother
explain it to you.

00:55:09.200 --> 00:55:12.620
Get the answers
to every question you have right now.

00:55:12.910 --> 00:55:14.660
From my mother?

00:55:14.660 --> 00:55:16.120
Don't worry.

00:55:16.120 --> 00:55:21.840
The only thing that I can truly consider
dear to me is you, Miyuki.

00:55:21.840 --> 00:55:25.930
And so from here on in,
I'm going to go on protecting you,

00:55:25.930 --> 00:55:28.640
and towards that end,
I'm going to come back here unscathed.

00:55:30.180 --> 00:55:35.640
Don't worry. There's nobody in this world
who can really hurt me.

00:55:49.780 --> 00:55:52.660
Ms. Miyuki?
Madam has regained consciousness.

00:55:53.660 --> 00:55:55.540
Oh, right!

00:56:02.670 --> 00:56:06.010
<i>The Airborne Unit
will soon arrive at its target point.</i>

00:56:06.550 --> 00:56:10.220
<i>Five enemy amphibious crafts
are now approaching the coastline.</i>

00:56:55.390 --> 00:56:57.930
That must be a nightmare
for the enemy soldiers.

00:56:58.520 --> 00:57:01.190
They should expect no less.

00:57:02.190 --> 00:57:06.820
Mother, there's something
I'd like to ask you.

00:57:08.400 --> 00:57:15.790
Just now, my brother said I was the only thing
he could truly consider dear to him.

00:57:16.120 --> 00:57:20.920
When I asked him why he said
"consider dear to him" rather than "dear to him,"

00:57:20.920 --> 00:57:26.000
he told me to have you explain it to me.

00:57:26.000 --> 00:57:28.920
Oh? Tatsuya said such a thing?

00:57:30.050 --> 00:57:33.470
I suppose this is as good a time
as ever to tell you.

00:57:33.470 --> 00:57:35.180
But before I do...

00:57:35.180 --> 00:57:40.560
you're to stop calling
that good-for-nothing "Brother."

00:57:42.100 --> 00:57:43.650
How can you say that?

00:57:43.980 --> 00:57:47.440
My brother just saved me
with that skill of his!

00:57:47.980 --> 00:57:49.570
You mean just now?

00:57:50.110 --> 00:57:52.450
That's the only thing he's capable of.

00:57:52.740 --> 00:57:54.320
The only thing?

00:57:54.700 --> 00:58:00.330
That boy, Tatsuya, was born
a defective magician.

00:58:01.250 --> 00:58:06.130
Magic is the ability to modify
information bodies and phenomena.

00:58:06.460 --> 00:58:08.880
But Tatsuya is unable to do those things.

00:58:08.880 --> 00:58:16.220
What he can do is to decompose information
bodies and then reassemble them. That's it.

00:58:17.100 --> 00:58:20.390
Being born without any talent for magic
in the truest sense of the word,

00:58:20.390 --> 00:58:24.850
the ability to alter an information element
into something else entirely

00:58:24.850 --> 00:58:28.400
makes that boy an unquestionably
defective magician.

00:58:28.820 --> 00:58:33.990
Well, although it was
that Regrowth skill that saved us.

00:58:34.530 --> 00:58:38.160
But to be precise,
that skill isn't actually magic.

00:58:39.160 --> 00:58:40.290
<i>Then...</i>

00:58:40.700 --> 00:58:43.040
<i>that skill of my brother's...</i>

00:58:43.910 --> 00:58:48.170
<i>If it's not magic, is it a miracle?</i>

00:58:48.500 --> 00:58:52.670
As magicians, we Yotsubas
are members of the Ten Master Clans,

00:58:52.670 --> 00:58:56.430
and no one can remain a Yotsuba
unless they're a magician.

00:58:56.430 --> 00:59:01.020
Being incapable of using magic,
that boy cannot live as a Yotsuba.

00:59:01.350 --> 00:59:09.400
That's why we, Maya and myself, decided
to subject him to a certain surgery seven years ago.

00:59:09.770 --> 00:59:11.940
The Artificial Magician Plan.

00:59:12.230 --> 00:59:18.200
A project in which a magician's abilities
are bestowed upon a non-magician

00:59:18.200 --> 00:59:21.490
by implanting an artificial
Magic Calculation Area into the brain.

00:59:23.160 --> 00:59:29.590
That mind-altering procedure resulted
in the loss of Tatsuya's emotions.

00:59:30.040 --> 00:59:34.840
No, perhaps "impulses"
is a better word than "emotions."

00:59:35.300 --> 00:59:42.470
Intense anger, deep sorrow, fierce jealousy,
grudges, hatred, excessive hunger,

00:59:42.470 --> 00:59:46.140
excessive sexual desire, blind love...

00:59:46.640 --> 00:59:49.610
Such impulses that would cause him
to forget himself...

00:59:49.610 --> 00:59:53.440
Save for one exception,
Tatsuya lost them all

00:59:53.440 --> 00:59:56.740
in exchange for gaining
the ability to wield magic.

00:59:58.280 --> 00:59:59.990
But no...

01:00:00.280 --> 01:00:01.740
Unfortunately,
in terms of performance...

01:00:02.120 --> 01:00:09.580
the artificial Magic Calculation Area is glaringly
inferior to the innate Magic Calculation Area.

01:00:12.630 --> 01:00:16.760
As it turned out, he could
only be useful as a Guardian.

01:00:17.430 --> 01:00:21.890
This operation...
Was it you who performed it, Mother?

01:00:22.350 --> 01:00:25.140
Who else but me could have?

01:00:30.270 --> 01:00:32.270
<i>Oh, I just realized something.</i>

01:00:32.820 --> 01:00:40.030
<i>That it wasn't just my brother who lost part
of his emotions thanks to that experiment.</i>

01:00:42.070 --> 01:00:43.530
Anyway,

01:00:43.530 --> 01:00:49.710
regarding why Tatsuya called you "what he truly considers
dear to him" rather than "someone dear to him"...

01:00:49.710 --> 01:00:52.170
Let me answer that question for you.

01:00:52.460 --> 01:00:54.550
No! I don't want to hear it!

01:00:55.050 --> 01:00:58.300
The one exception,
what Tatsuya didn't lose...

01:00:58.630 --> 01:00:59.760
That's your answer.

01:00:59.760 --> 01:01:01.300
Please stop!

01:01:01.590 --> 01:01:05.970
The one impulse that remained inside him
was his love for his sister.

01:01:05.970 --> 01:01:10.190
To love his little sister, in other words, you,
and to try to protect you.

01:01:10.190 --> 01:01:12.690
That's enough, Mother!

01:01:12.690 --> 01:01:16.940
That is the one genuine emotion
left inside him.

01:01:19.740 --> 01:01:22.820
Since Tatsuya knows all about himself,

01:01:22.820 --> 01:01:26.830
that must be what he meant
when he said, "consider to be dear."

01:01:27.200 --> 01:01:31.250
As for me, he merely recognizes me
as his mother,

01:01:31.250 --> 01:01:35.340
but the natural love between parent
and child doesn't exist between us.

01:01:35.960 --> 01:01:41.470
Did you choose for that
to happen intentionally, Mother?

01:01:41.470 --> 01:01:44.680
I did feel that if he could keep one impulse,

01:01:44.680 --> 01:01:48.600
it should be love for you.

01:01:51.890 --> 01:01:57.110
<i>How can I ever repay my brother?</i>

01:01:57.530 --> 01:02:00.110
<i>What is it that I can give him in return?</i>

01:02:01.820 --> 01:02:07.910
<i>As it is now, even this life of mine
was given to me by my brother.</i>

01:02:09.330 --> 01:02:12.750
Do you have any other questions?

01:02:14.420 --> 01:02:15.420
No.

01:02:16.040 --> 01:02:18.000
Thank you very much.

01:02:27.010 --> 01:02:29.140
The Irregular at Magic High School:
Reminiscence Arc

01:02:30.060 --> 01:02:32.890
The ship shadow of what appears
to be a detached force from the enemy fleet

01:02:32.890 --> 01:02:35.100
is now approaching
from northern Agunijima!

01:02:35.440 --> 01:02:36.610
What did you say?

01:02:36.940 --> 01:02:40.360
The enemy fleet consists
of two high-speed cruisers and four destroyers.

01:02:40.820 --> 01:02:44.240
This base will fall
within the enemy's range in 20 minutes!

01:02:44.240 --> 01:02:45.530
Where's our backup?

01:02:45.530 --> 01:02:48.620
Four flight platoons
have taken off from Nyutabaru!

01:02:49.160 --> 01:02:50.910
Approximate ETA, 20 minutes!

01:02:51.370 --> 01:02:55.040
We're cutting it close, huh? What's the status
of our counterattack on the enemy fleet?

01:02:55.290 --> 01:02:58.540
Our defense unit is engaging with the enemy
in the waters around the Kerama Islands!

01:02:59.550 --> 01:03:01.920
What's the Navy doing, anyway?

01:03:02.300 --> 01:03:07.180
Order the Airborne Unit now fighting
the enemy ground troops to withdraw!

01:03:15.810 --> 01:03:18.810
The battle doesn't seem
to be going well, does it?

01:03:24.110 --> 01:03:25.950
You can't possibly reach them.

01:03:26.280 --> 01:03:28.910
What on earth are you planning to do?

01:03:34.790 --> 01:03:35.790
What's that?

01:03:37.540 --> 01:03:40.040
Madam, I have a request.

01:03:40.420 --> 01:03:41.670
What could that be?

01:03:41.880 --> 01:03:44.380
I'd like to go meet Tatsuya.

01:03:45.170 --> 01:03:48.890
Honami, you're my bodyguard,
aren't you?

01:03:49.180 --> 01:03:50.930
Please forgive me.

01:03:51.260 --> 01:03:52.310
However...

01:03:54.180 --> 01:03:55.850
Well, fine.

01:03:55.850 --> 01:04:00.690
Since it looks like Tatsuya's planning to do
that thing, why don't you go ahead and help him?

01:04:00.900 --> 01:04:02.400
Thank you very much!

01:04:03.440 --> 01:04:06.820
Um, what do you mean by "that thing"?

01:04:06.820 --> 01:04:09.780
He only knows
that it's theoretically possible,

01:04:09.780 --> 01:04:15.660
and has yet to actually try it,
but that boy seems to have a plan.

01:04:18.540 --> 01:04:20.750
Both of you, please return to base.

01:04:21.000 --> 01:04:23.130
I'll be fine on my own.

01:04:23.550 --> 01:04:26.090
Don't be ridiculous!
You need to come back with us, too.

01:04:26.260 --> 01:04:31.100
I can't do that. The base won't be safe
until I destroy the enemy fleet.

01:04:32.100 --> 01:04:33.850
For your family's sake?

01:04:35.930 --> 01:04:38.850
If that's the case,
then at least get away from here.

01:04:39.100 --> 01:04:43.980
I can't. There's no time
to search for another firing point.

01:04:47.650 --> 01:04:50.110
Then, we'll be staying, too.

01:04:50.910 --> 01:04:54.870
Even if you become
collateral damage if I fail?

01:04:55.200 --> 01:04:58.580
There's no strategy that's 100% failsafe,

01:04:58.580 --> 01:05:02.080
just as there are no battlefields
with zero risk of death.

01:05:02.380 --> 01:05:06.840
If victory or defeat is incidental to warfare,
then life or death is incidental to soldiers.

01:05:14.640 --> 01:05:17.060
Sanada, we're going to thwart them!

01:05:17.060 --> 01:05:17.770
Sir!

01:05:18.100 --> 01:05:21.150
Shiba, you focus on magic
for attacking the fleet!

01:05:53.510 --> 01:05:55.470
This doesn't look good, does it?

01:05:55.470 --> 01:05:57.470
Damn you! Don't lose heart now!

01:05:57.680 --> 01:06:03.440
That's easy for you to say, Captain,
but I've always had a speed problem.

01:06:05.190 --> 01:06:09.570
<i>Calculating the trajectory of the bullet
that landed in the center of the enemy fleet.</i>

01:06:28.500 --> 01:06:30.050
I'll help you!

01:06:38.850 --> 01:06:41.980
This force is comparable
to that of the Jumonji clan!

01:06:41.980 --> 01:06:45.980
But using magic so recklessly,
how long can her body hold up?

01:06:47.570 --> 01:06:49.730
Trajectory calculations complete.

01:06:58.620 --> 01:07:01.290
<i>Material Burst... Activate.</i>

01:07:11.260 --> 01:07:14.470
Neutralization of enemy fleet... Done.

01:07:14.970 --> 01:07:18.050
Master Tatsuya, good job.

01:07:18.760 --> 01:07:20.010
Ms. Honami!

01:07:21.520 --> 01:07:22.730
It's a tsunami!

01:07:46.370 --> 01:07:49.130
It's all right, Tatsuya.

01:07:50.210 --> 01:07:52.710
I've reached the end of my life.

01:07:52.710 --> 01:07:54.260
No, you're...

01:07:54.590 --> 01:07:56.630
It's not your fault.

01:07:56.880 --> 01:08:02.010
There's no telling when we Augmented
Magicians will exhaust our lifespans.

01:08:04.140 --> 01:08:08.810
I was tasked with the duty of serving
as a shield from before I was born,

01:08:09.270 --> 01:08:11.900
and today I fulfilled that duty in full.

01:08:12.940 --> 01:08:17.410
And I finished it all
not because of someone's order,

01:08:17.410 --> 01:08:19.660
but of my own volition.

01:08:21.830 --> 01:08:23.660
Please don't do that.

01:08:24.290 --> 01:08:29.540
Until now, I never had any freedom
to choose how I would live my life,

01:08:29.920 --> 01:08:33.920
but today I was able
to choose where to die.

01:08:34.510 --> 01:08:37.220
I have no desire
to pass up a chance like that.

01:08:37.760 --> 01:08:41.180
Now I can die as a human...

01:08:41.510 --> 01:08:44.520
rather than as a man-made instrument.

01:08:45.220 --> 01:08:48.190
So please, just let me die now.

01:09:13.460 --> 01:09:16.510
AUGUST 17, A.D. 2096

01:09:26.270 --> 01:09:29.850
OKINAWA NAVAL BATTLE MEMORIAL

01:09:37.940 --> 01:09:40.610
<i>After that...</i>

01:09:40.610 --> 01:09:42.700
<i>Honami didn't return.</i>

01:09:44.120 --> 01:09:45.240
JOINT FUNERAL FOR OKINAWA
NAVAL BATTLE CASUALTIES

01:09:53.170 --> 01:09:55.380
<i>In accordance with
Honami's own wishes...</i>

01:09:56.130 --> 01:10:00.590
<i>her cremated remains
were all scattered into the ocean.</i>

01:10:01.300 --> 01:10:05.100
<i>As I gazed at Honami's ashes
being carried away by the wind,</i>

01:10:05.430 --> 01:10:07.640
<i>I realized something.</i>

01:10:08.430 --> 01:10:11.940
<i>That day, I had died at one point.</i>

01:10:12.270 --> 01:10:15.190
<i>I lost the life
that my mother had given me,</i>

01:10:15.610 --> 01:10:19.280
<i>and was granted a new life
by my brother!</i>

01:10:19.280 --> 01:10:22.280
<i>And so, I belong
completely to my brother.</i>

01:10:24.740 --> 01:10:25.780
What's the matter?

01:10:26.780 --> 01:10:28.370
It's nothing.

01:10:30.040 --> 01:10:32.000
The wind is getting stronger.

01:10:32.330 --> 01:10:33.870
Let's head back.

01:10:33.870 --> 01:10:35.580
Yes, Brother!

01:10:48.470 --> 01:10:49.680
<i>Brother...</i>

01:10:50.060 --> 01:10:51.680
<i>wherever you go...</i>

01:10:52.270 --> 01:10:53.600
<i>no matter how far...</i>

01:10:54.020 --> 01:10:56.230
<i>I will follow you!</i>
